{
  "title": "Bidding Farewell (Wida) to Imam Husayn (a.s.) — Karbala",
  "code": "012",
  "slug": "farewell-imam-hussain-karbala",
  "data": "Twentieth: Farewell ziyarat\nSayyid Ibn Tawus says that it is recommended for those who intend to leave the holy shrine of Imam al-Husayn (`a) after they have accomplished visiting his tomb to throw themselves on the tomb, kiss it, and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَوْلاَيَ\nalssalamu `alayka ya mawlaya\nPeace be upon you, O my master.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُجَّةَ ٱللَّهِ\nalssalamu `alayka ya hujjata allahi\nPeace be upon you, O Allah’s Argument (against His creatures).\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صِفْوَةَ ٱللَّهِ\nalssalamu `alayka ya safwata allahi\nPeace be upon you, O Allah’s choice.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَالِصَةَ ٱللَّهِ\nalssalamu `alayka ya khalisata allahi\nPeace be upon you, O Allah’s select.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا قَتِيلَ ٱلظَّمَاءِ\nalssalamu `alayka ya qatila alzzama'i\nPeace be upon you, O victim of thirst.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا غَرِيبَ ٱلْغُرَبَاءِ\nalssalamu `alayka ya ghariba alghuraba'i\nPeace be upon you, O strangest of all strangers.\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ سَلاَمَ مُوَدِّع\nalssalamu `alayka salama muwaddi`in\nPeace be upon you; this is the greeting of one who has to bid farewell to you\nلاََ سَئِمٍ وَلاَ قَالٍ\nla sa'imin wa la qalin\nalthough he is neither bored with you nor tired of you.\nفَإِنْ امْضِ فَلاَ عَنْ مَلاَلَةٍ\nfa'in amdi fala `an malalatin\nIf I leave (you), this is not because of weariness;\nوَإِنْ اقِمْ فَلاَ عَنْ سُوءِ ظَنٍّ بِمَا وَعَدَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلصَّابِرِينَ\nwa in uqim fala `an su'i zannin bima wa`ada allahu alssabirina\nand if I reside, this is not because of mistrusting the promise that Allah has made for the serene ones.\nلاََ جَعَلَهُ ٱللَّهُ آخِرَ ٱلْعَهْدِ مِنِّي لِزِيَارَتِكَ\nla ja`alahu allahu akhira al`ahdi minni liziyaratika\nMay Allah not decide this time of my visit to be the last.\nوَرَزَقَنِيَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْعَوْدَ إِلَىٰ مَشْهَدِكَ\nwa razaqaniya allahu al`awda ila mashhadika\nMay He endue me with more chances to return to your shrine,\nوَٱلْمَقَامَ بِفَنَائِكَ\nwalmaqama bifina'ika\nto reside in your courtyard,\nوَٱلْقِيَامَ فِي حَرَمِكَ\nwalqiyama fi haramika\nand to stay in your sanctuary.\nوَإِيَّاهُ اسْالُ انْ يُسْعِدَنِي بِكُمْ\nwa iyyahu as'alu an yus`idani bikum\nTo Him do I pray to make me delightful with you\nوَيَجْعَلَنِي مَعَكُمْ فِي ٱلدُّنْيَا وَٱلآخِرَةِ\nwa yaj`alani ma`akum fi alddunya wal-akhirati\nand to include me with you in this world and in the Hereafter.\nOther Farewell Ziarats from Book Nibrās al-Zāʼir fī Ziyārat al-Ḥāʼir\nImam al-Sadiq (peace be upon him) said: If you want to bid him farewell, say:\nالسَّلامُ عَلَيْكَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ،\nAs-salāmu ʿalayka wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuhu,\nPeace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings,\nأَسْتَوْدِعُكَ اللّهَ وَأَقْرَأُ عَلَيْكَ السَّلامُ،\nAstawdiʿuka Allāh wa aqraʾu ʿalayka as-salām,\nI entrust you to Allah and convey my greetings to you,\nآمَنَّا بِاللّهِ وَبِالرَّسُولِ وَبِمَا جِئْتَ بِهِ وَدَلَلْتَ عَلَيْهِ،\nĀmannā bi-Allāh wa bi-rasūl wa bimā jiʾta bihi wa dalalta ʿalayh,\nWe believe in Allah and the Messenger and in what you brought and guided to,\nوَاتَّبَعْنَا الرَّسُولَ فَاكْتُبْنَا مَعَ الشَّاهِدِينَ،\nWa-ttabaʿnā ar-rasūl fa-uktubnā maʿa ash-shāhidīn,\nAnd we followed the Messenger, so write us among the witnesses,\nاَللّهُمَّ لاَ تَجْعَلْهُ آخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنَّا وَمِنْهُ،\nAllāhumma lā tajʿalhu ākhir al-ʿahd minnā wa minhu,\nO Allah, do not make this the last of our visit and his visit,\nاَللّهُمَّ إِنَّا نَسْأَلُكَ أَنْ تَنْفَعَنَا بِحُبِّهِ،\nAllāhumma innā nasʾaluka an tanfaʿanā bi-ḥubbihi,\nO Allah, we ask You to benefit us with his love,\nاَللّهُمَّ ابْعَثْهُ مَقَاماً مَحْمُوداً تَنْصُرُ بِهِ دِينَكَ،\nAllāhumma ibʿathhu maqāman maḥmūdan tanṣuru bihi dīnak,\nO Allah, raise him to a praised station by which You support Your religion,\nوَتَقْتُلُ بِهِ عَدُوَّكَ،\nWa taqtulu bihi ʿaduwwaka,\nAnd by which You kill Your enemy,\nوَتُبِيدُ بِهِ مَنْ نَصَبَ حَرْباً لِآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ،\nWa tubīdu bihi man naṣaba ḥarban li-Āl Muḥammad,\nAnd annihilate with it those who waged war against the family of Muhammad,\nفَإِنَّكَ وَعَدْتَهُ ذلِكَ،\nFa-innaka waʿadtahu dhālika,\nFor You have promised him that,\nوَأَنْتَ لاَ تُخْلِفُ الْمِيعَادَ،\nWa-anta lā tukhlifu al-mīʿād,\nAnd You do not break Your promise,\nالسَّلامُ عَلَيْكَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ،\nAs-salāmu ʿalayka wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuhu,\nPeace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings,\nأَشْهَدُ أَنَّكُمْ شُهَدَاءٌ نُجَبَاءٌ،\nAshhadu annakum shuhadāʾun nujabāʾ,\nI bear witness that you are noble martyrs,\nجَاهَدْتُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللّهِ،\nJāhadttum fī sabīl Allāh,\nYou struggled in the way of Allah,\nوَقُتِلْتُمْ عَلَى مِنْهَاجِ رَسُولِ اللّهِ،\nWaqutilttum ʿalā minhāj Rasūl Allāh,\nAnd you were killed on the path of the Messenger of Allah,\nصَلَّى اللّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهِ وَابْنِ رَسُولِهِ،\nṢallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa ālih wa ibn Rasūlihi,\nMay Allah's blessings be upon him and his family and the son of his Messenger,\nصَلَّى اللّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهِ،\nṢallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa ālih,\nMay Allah's blessings be upon him and his family,\nأَنْتُمُ السَّابِقُونَ وَالْمُهَاجِرُونَ وَالْأَنْصَارُ،\nAntum as-sābiqūn wal-muhājirūn wal-anṣār,\nYou are the pioneers, the emigrants, and the supporters,\nأَشْهَدُ أَنَّكُمْ أَنْصَارُ اللّهِ،\nAshhadu annakum anṣāru Allāh,\nI bear witness that you are the helpers of Allah,\nوَأَنْصَارُ رَسُولِهِ،\nWa anṣāru Rasūlihi,\nAnd the helpers of His Messenger,\nصَلَّى اللّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهِ،\nṢallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa ālih,\nMay Allah's blessings be upon him and his family,\nفَالْحَمْدُ لِلّهِ الَّذِي صَدَقَكُمْ وَعْدَهُ،\nFa-al-ḥamdu li-Allāh alladhī ṣadaqakum waʿdahu,\nSo all praise be to Allah who fulfilled His promise to you,\nوَأَرَاكُمْ مَا تُحِبُّونَ،\nWa arākum mā tuḥibbūn,\nAnd showed you what you love,\nوَصَلَّى اللّهُ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ،\nWa ṣallā Allāhu ʿalā Muḥammad wa āl Muḥammad,\nAnd may Allah's blessings be upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ،\nWa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuhu,\nAnd the mercy of Allah and His blessings,\nاَللّهُمَّ لاَ تَشْغَلْنِي فِي الدُّنْيَا عَنْ ذِكْرِ نِعْمَتِكَ،\nAllāhumma lā tashghalnī fī ad-dunyā ʿan dhikr niʿmatika,\nO Allah, do not preoccupy me in this world from remembering Your bounty,\nلاَ بِإِكْثَارٍ تُلْهِينِي عَجَائِبُ بَهْجَتِهَا،\nLā bi-ikthār tunhilnī ʿajāʾib bahjatihā,\nNot by abundance that its wonders distract me,\nوَتَفْتِنِّي زَهَرَاتُ زِينَتِهَا،\nWa taftinnī zaharāt zīnatihā,\nAnd its flowers of adornment tempt me,\nوَلاَ بِاِقْلاَلٍ يَضُرُّ بِعَمَلِي كَدُّهُ،\nWa lā bi-iqlāl yaḍurru bi-ʿamalī kadduhu,\nNor by scarcity that its hardship harms my deeds,\nوَيَمْلَأُ صَدْرِي هَمُّهُ،\nWa yamlaʾu ṣadrī hammuhu,\nAnd fills my chest with its worries,\nأَعْطِنِي مِنْ ذلِكَ غِنىً عَنْ شِرَارِ خَلْقِكَ،\nAʿṭinī min dhālika ghinā ʿan shirār khalqik,\nGrant me from that wealth to suffice me from the wicked of Your creation,\nوَبَلاَغاً أَنَالُ بِهِ رِضَاكَ،\nWa balāghan anālu bihi riḍāk,\nAnd a reach by which I attain Your pleasure,\nيَا أَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ،\nYā arḥama ar-rāḥimīn,\nO Most Merciful of the merciful,\nوَصَلَّى اللّهُ عَلَى رَسُولِهِ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللّهِ،\nWa ṣallā Allāhu ʿalā Rasūlihi Muḥammad bin ʿAbd Allāh,\nAnd may Allah's blessings be upon His Messenger Muhammad bin ʿAbd Allāh,\nوَعَلَى أَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ الطَّيِّبِينَ الْأخْيَارِ،\nWa ʿalā ahl baytihi aṭ-ṭayyibīn al-akhyār,\nAnd upon his good and righteous family,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ.\nWa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuhu,\nAnd the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nShaykh al-Mufid, said: The farewell is that you come to the grave and stand over it as you stood at the beginning of the visit, and face it and say:\nالسَّلامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَلِيَّ اللّهِ،\nAs-salāmu ʿalayka yā waliyy Allāh,\nPeace be upon you, O friend of Allah,\nالسَّلامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا أَبَا عَبْدِ اللّهِ،\nAs-salāmu ʿalayka yā Abā ʿAbd Allāh,\nPeace be upon you, O Abā ʿAbd Allāh,\nأَنْتَ لِي جُنَّةٌ مِنَ الْعَذَابِ،\nAnta lī junnatun min al-ʿadhāb,\nYou are for me a shield from punishment,\nوَهذَا أَوَانُ انْصِرَافِي عَنْكَ،\nWa hādhā awān insirāfī ʿanka,\nAnd this is the time of my departure from you,\nغَيْرَ رَاغِبٍ عَنْكَ،\nGhayra rāghib ʿanka,\nNot desiring anyone else,\nوَلاَ مُسْتَبْدِلٍ بِكَ سِوَاكَ،\nWa lā mustabdil bika siwāk,\nNor exchanging you for another,\nوَلاَ مُؤْثِرٍ عَلَيْكَ غَيْرَكَ،\nWa lā muʾthir ʿalayk ghayrak,\nNor preferring anyone over you,\nوَلاَ زَاهِدٍ فِي قُرْبِكَ،\nWa lā zāhid fī qurbik,\nNor being uninterested in being close to you,\nوَجُدْتُ بِنَفْسِي لِلْحَدَثَانِ،\nWa judtu binafsī lil-ḥadathān,\nAnd I have given myself for the events,\nوَتَرَكْتُ الْأَهْلَ وَالْأَوْطَانَ،\nWa taraktu al-ahl wa al-awṭān,\nAnd left my family and homeland,\nفَكُنْ لِي يَوْمَ حَاجَتِي،\nFakunn lī yawma ḥājatī,\nSo be for me on the day of my need,\nوَفَقْرِي وَفَاقَتِي،\nWa faqri wa faqātī,\nAnd my poverty and destitution,\nوَيَوْمَ لاَ يُغْنِي عَنِّي وَالِدِي وَوَلَدِي،\nWa yawma lā yughni ʿannī wālidī wa waladī,\nAnd on the day when neither my father nor my son will avail me,\nوَلاَ حَمِيمِي وَلاَ قَرِيبِي،\nWa lā ḥamīmī wa lā qarībī,\nNor my close friend nor my relative,\nأَسْأَلُ اللّهَ الَّذِي قَدَّرَ وَخَلَقَ،\nAsʾalu Allāh alladhī qaddara wa khalaq,\nI ask Allah, who has decreed and created,\nأَنْ يُنَفِّسَ بِكَ كَرْبِي،\nAn yunaffisa bika karbī,\nTo relieve my distress through you,\nوَأَسْأَلُ اللّهَ الَّذِي قَدَّرَ عَلَيَّ فِرَاقَ مَكَانِكَ،\nWa asʾalu Allāh alladhī qaddara ʿalayya firāqa makānika,\nAnd I ask Allah, who has decreed upon me the separation from your place,\nأَنْ لاَ يَجْعَلَهُ آخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنِّي وَمِنْ رَجْعَتِي،\nAn lā yajʿalahu ākhir al-ʿahd minnī wa min rajʿatī,\nTo not make it the last of my visit and my return,\nوَأَسْأَلُ اللّهَ الَّذِي أَبْكَى عَلَيْكَ عَيْنِي،\nWa asʾalu Allāh alladhī abkā ʿalayka ʿaynī,\nAnd I ask Allah, who made my eyes cry over you,\nأَنْ يَجْعَلَهُ سَنَداً لِي،\nAn yajʿalahu sanadan lī,\nTo make it a support for me,\nوَأَسْأَلُ اللّهَ الَّذِي نَقَلَنِي إِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَحْلِي وَأَهْلِي،\nWa asʾalu Allāh alladhī naqalnī ilayka min raḥlī wa ahlī,\nAnd I ask Allah, who brought me to you from my journey and my family,\nأَنْ يَجْعَلَهُ ذُخْراً لِي،\nAn yajʿalahu dhukhran lī,\nTo make it a treasure for me,\nوَأَسْأَلُ اللّهَ الَّذِي أَرَانِي مَكَانَكَ،\nWa asʾalu Allāh alladhī arānī makānak,\nAnd I ask Allah, who showed me your place,\nوَهَدَانِي لِلتَّسْلِيمِ عَلَيْكَ،\nWa hadānī li-taslīm ʿalayk,\nAnd guided me to greet you,\nوَلِزِيَارَتِي إِيَّاكَ،\nWa li-ziyāratī īyyāk,\nAnd to visit you,\nأَنْ يُورِدَنِي حَوْضَكُمْ،\nAn yūridnī ḥawḍakum,\nTo bring me to your pool,\nوَيَرْزُقَنِي مُرَافَقَتَكُمْ فِي الْجِنَانِ،\nWa yarzuqanī murāfaqatakum fī al-jinān,\nAnd grant me your companionship in the gardens,\nمَعَ آبَائِكَ الصَّالِحِينَ،\nMaʿa ābāʾika aṣ-ṣāliḥīn,\nWith your righteous fathers,\nصَلَّى اللّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ أَجْمَعِينَ،\nṢallā Allāhu ʿalayhim ajmaʿīn,\nMay Allah's blessings be upon them all,\nالسَّلامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَفْوَةَ اللّهِ،\nAs-salāmu ʿalayka yā ṣafwat Allāh,\nPeace be upon you, O chosen one of Allah,\nالسَّلامُ عَلَى مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللّهِ\nAs-salāmu ʿalā Muḥammad bin ʿAbd Allāh,\nPeace be upon Muhammad bin ʿAbd Allah,\nحَبِيبِ اللّهِ وَصَفْوَتِهِ،\nḤabīb Allāh wa ṣafwatih,\nThe beloved of Allah and His chosen one,\nوَأَمِينِهِ وَرَسُولِهِ،\nWa amīnih wa rasūlih,\nHis trustworthy one and His messenger,\nوَسَيِّدِ النَّبِيّينَ،\nWa sayyid an-nabiyyīn,\nAnd the master of the prophets,\nالسَّلامُ عَلَى أَمِيرِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ،\nAs-salāmu ʿalā Amīr al-Muʾminīn,\nPeace be upon the Commander of the Faithful,\nوَصِيِّ رَسُولِ اللّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ،\nWaṣiyy Rasūl Allāh Rabb al-ʿālamīn,\nThe successor of the Messenger of Allah, the Lord of the worlds,\nوَقَائِدِ الْغُرِّ الْمُحَجَّلِينَ،\nWa qāʾid al-ghurr al-muḥajjalīn,\nAnd the leader of the bright-faced ones,\nالسَّلامُ عَلَى الْأَئِمَّةِ الرَّاشِدِينَ الْمَهْدِيّينَ،\nAs-salāmu ʿalā al-aʾimma ar-rāshidīn al-mahdīyīn,\nPeace be upon the rightly guided Imams,\nالسَّلامُ عَلَى مَنْ فِي الْحَيْرِ مِنْكُمْ،\nAs-salāmu ʿalā man fī al-ḥayr minkum,\nPeace be upon those among you in the shrine,\nالسَّلامُ عَلَى مَلاَئِكَةِ اللّهِ الْبَاقِينَ الْمُقِيمِينَ،\nAs-salāmu ʿalā malāʾikat Allāh al-bāqīn al-muqīmīn,\nPeace be upon the remaining and residing angels of Allah,\nالْمُسَبِّحِينَ الَّذِينَ هُمْ بِأَمْرِ رَبِّهِمْ قَائِمُونَ،\nAl-musabbiḥīn alladhīna hum bi-amri rabbihim qāʾimūn,\nThose who glorify Him and stand by the command of their Lord,\nالسَّلامُ عَلَيْنَا وَعَلَى عِبَادِ اللّهِ الصَّالِحِينَ،\nAs-salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibād Allāh aṣ-ṣāliḥīn,\nPeace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah,\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ.\nWa al-ḥamdu li-Allāh Rabbi al-ʿālamīn.\nAnd all praise is due to Allah, the Lord of the worlds.\nوتقول:\nWa taqūl:\nAnd you say:\nسَلامُ اللّهِ وَسَلامُ مَلائِكَتِهِ الْمُقَرَّبِينَ،\nSalām Allāh wa salām malāʾikatihi al-muqarrabīn,\nPeace of Allah and the peace of His close angels,\nوَأَنبِيائِهِ الْمُرْسَلِينَ،\nWa anbiyāʾihi al-mursalīn,\nAnd His sent prophets,\nوَعِبادِهِ الصَّالِحِينَ،\nWa ʿibādihi aṣ-ṣāliḥīn,\nAnd His righteous servants,\nيَابْنَ رَسُولِ اللّهِ،\nYā ibn Rasūl Allāh,\nO son of the Messenger of Allah,\nعَلَيْكَ وَعَلَى رُوحِكَ وَبَدَنِكَ،\nʿAlayka wa ʿalā rūḥik wa badanik,\nUpon you and upon your soul and body,\nوَعَلَى ذُرِّيَّتِكَ،\nWa ʿalā dhurriyyatik,\nAnd upon your descendants,\nوَمَنْ حَضَرَكَ مِنْ أَوْلِيَائِكَ،\nWa man ḥaḍaraka min awliyāʾik,\nAnd those who are present with you from your friends,\nأَسْتَوْدِعُكَ اللّهَ وَأَسْتَرْعِيكَ،\nAstawdiʿuka Allāh wa astarʿīk,\nI entrust you to Allah and I seek His protection for you,\nوَأَقْرَأُ عَلَيْكَ السَّلامُ،\nWa aqraʾu ʿalayka as-salām,\nAnd I convey my greetings to you,\nآمَنَّا بِاللّهِ،\nĀmannā bi-Allāh,\nWe believed in Allah,\nوَبِرَسُولِ اللّهِ،\nWa bi-rasūl Allāh,\nAnd in the Messenger of Allah,\nوَبِمَا جَاءَ بِهِ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّهِ،\nWa bimā jāʾa bihi min ʿindi Allāh,\nAnd in what he brought from Allah,\nاَللّهُمَّ اكْتُبْنَا مَعَ الشَّاهِدِينَ.\nAllāhumma uktubnā maʿa ash-shāhidīn.\nO Allah, write us among the witnesses.\nوتقول:\nWa taqūl:\nAnd you say:\nاَللّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ،\nAllāhumma ṣalli ʿalā Muḥammad wa āl Muḥammad,\nO Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَلاَ تَجْعَلْهُ آخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنْ زِيَارَتِي ابْنَ رَسُولِكَ،\nWa lā tajʿalahu ākhir al-ʿahd min ziyāratī ibn Rasūlik,\nAnd do not make this the last of my visit to the son of Your Messenger,\nوَارْزُقْنِي زِيَارَتَهُ أَبَداً مَا أَبْقَيْتَنِي،\nWa urzuqnī ziyāratah abadan mā abqaytanī,\nAnd grant me his visit forever as long as You keep me,\nاَللّهُمَّ وَانْفَعْنِي بِحُبِّهِ يَا رَبَّ الْعَالَمِينَ،\nAllāhumma wanfaʿnī bi-ḥubbihi yā Rabba al-ʿālamīn,\nO Allah, benefit me with his love, O Lord of the worlds,\nاَللّهُمَّ ابْعَثْهُ مَقَاماً مَحْمُوداً،\nAllāhumma ibʿathhu maqāman maḥmūdan,\nO Allah, raise him to a praised station,\nإِنَّكَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ،\nInnaka ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr,\nIndeed, You are capable of all things,\nاَللّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ بَعْدَ الصَّلاَةِ وَالتَّسْلِيمِ،\nAllāhumma innī asʾaluk baʿda aṣ-ṣalāt wa at-taslīm,\nO Allah, I ask You after prayer and greeting,\nأَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ،\nAn tuṣallī ʿalā Muḥammad wa āl Muḥammad,\nTo send blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَأَنْ لاَ تَجْعَلَهُ آخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنْ زِيَارَتِي إِيَّاهُ،\nWa an lā tajʿalahu ākhir al-ʿahd min ziyāratī īyyāh,\nAnd not to make it the last of my visit to him,\nفَإِنْ جَعَلْتَهُ يَا رَبِّ فَاحْشُرْنِي مَعَهُ،\nFa-in jaʿaltahu yā Rabb faḥshurnī maʿah,\nIf You make it so, O Lord, then gather me with him,\nوَمَعَ آبَائِهِ وَأَوْلِيَائِهِ،\nWa maʿa ābāʾih wa awliyāʾih,\nAnd with his fathers and friends,\nوَإِنْ أَبْقَيْتَنِي يَا رَبِّ،\nWa in abqaytanī yā Rabb,\nAnd if You keep me, O Lord,\nفَارْزُقْنِي الْعَوْدَ إِلَيْهِ،\nFa urzuqnī al-ʿawd ilayh,\nThen grant me the return to him,\nثُمَّ الْعَوْدَ إِلَيْهِ بَعْدَ الْعَوْدِ،\nThumma al-ʿawd ilayh baʿd al-ʿawd,\nAnd then return to him after return,\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَا أَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ،\nBi-raḥmatika yā arḥama ar-rāḥimīn,\nBy Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful,\nاَللّهُمَّ اجْعَلْ لِي لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ فِي أَوْلِيَائِكَ،\nAllāhumma ijʿal lī lisān ṣidq fī awliyāʾik,\nO Allah, make for me a truthful tongue among Your friends,\nوَحَبِّبْ إِلَيَّ مَشَاهِدَهُمْ،\nWa ḥabbib ilayya mashāhidahum,\nAnd make their places beloved to me,\nاَللّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ،\nAllāhumma ṣalli ʿalā Muḥammad wa āl Muḥammad,\nO Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَلاَ تَشْغَلْنِي عَنْ ذِكْرِكَ،\nWa lā tashghalnī ʿan dhikrik,\nAnd do not preoccupy me from Your remembrance,\nبِإِكْثَارٍ عَلَيَّ مِنَ الدُّنْيَا،\nBi-ikthār ʿalayya min ad-dunyā,\nBy increasing upon me from the world,\nتُلْهِينِي عَجَائِبُ بَهْجَتِهَا،\nTulhīnī ʿajāʾib bahjatihā,\nIts wonders distract me,\nوَتَفْتِنِّي زَهَرَاتُ زِينَتِهَا،\nWa taftinnī zaharāt zīnatihā,\nAnd its flowers of adornment tempt me,\nوَلاَ بِإِقْلاَلٍ يَضُرُّ بِعَمَلِي كَدُّهُ،\nWa lā bi-iqlāl yaḍurru bi-ʿamalī kadduhu,\nNor by scarcity that its hardship harms my deeds,\nوَيَمْلَأُ صَدْرِي هَمُّهُ،\nWa yamlaʾu ṣadrī hammuhu,\nAnd fills my chest with its worries,\nأَعْطِنِي مِنْ ذلِكَ غِنىً عَنْ أَشْرَارِ خَلْقِكَ،\nAʿṭinī min dhālika ghinan ʿan ashrār khalqik,\nGrant me from that wealth to suffice me from the wicked of Your creation,\nوَبَلاَغاً أَنَالُ بِهِ رِضَاكَ،\nWa balāghan anālu bihi riḍāk,\nAnd a reach by which I attain Your pleasure,\nيَا رَحْمَنُ.\nYā Raḥmān,\nO Most Merciful.\nاَلسَّلامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَا مَلاَئِكَةَ اللّهِ،\nAs-salāmu ʿalaykum yā malāʾikat Allāh,\nPeace be upon you, O angels of Allah,\nوَزُوَّارَ قَبْرِ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللّهِ.\nWa zuwwār qabr Abī ʿAbd Allāh,\nAnd visitors of the grave of Abā ʿAbd Allāh.\nThen place your right cheek on the grave once, And the left once, And insist in supplication and request, When you leave, do not turn your face away from the grave until you exit."
}
